EPA SWMM (Storm Water Management Model), computational engine

The SWMM engine is a work of the United States Environmental Protection Agency
(EPA). Works authored by US federal government employees are not subject to
copyright in the United States (17 USC 105); EPA distributes the SWMM engine as
public domain software. See https://www.epa.gov/water-research/storm-water-management-model-swmm

What is in this folder:
- swmm5.js / swmm5.wasm: the SWMM 5.2.4 engine compiled to WebAssembly with
  Emscripten 3.1.64, built from EPA's source at tag v5.2.4 by
  tools/build_swmm_wasm.sh in this repository. The binary reports version
  52004 (5.2.4) through its API; the node test C0 checks that.
- SWMM_Readme.txt: the readme from EPA's SWMM 5.2.2 engine source archive,
  kept for provenance. It does not describe the shipped binary (see the note
  at the top of that file).
